            "otherCytogenetics": "BCR/ABL/ASS: 72/100 cells had a variant abnormal fusion reflecting a single BCR/ABL fusion. The Philadelphia rearrangement was not visible in the metaphase karyotype  and is, thus, likely a cryptic rearrangement involving at least three chromosomes.    (Twenty-one cells (21%) had three signals for ASS and ABL with  no fusion signal.) | RUNX1T1: \u00c2\u00a089/100 cells (89%) had three signals, consistent with the trisomy  8 in the metaphase karyotype. \u00c2\u00a0There was no evidence for RUNX1T1/RUNX1  fusion. \u00c2\u00a0In addition, 80% of cells had three chromosome 8 centromere  signals, also consistent with trisomy 8. | DEK/NUP21: \u00c2\u00a096/100 cells (96%) had three signals for both probes,  consistent with trisomies 6 and 9 in the metaphase karyotype. \u00c2\u00a0There was no evidence for DEK/NUP21 fusion | PML: \u00c2\u00a041/100 cells (41%) had three signals, consistent with the trisomy 15  in the metaphase karyotype. \u00c2\u00a0Fifty-two cells (52%) had four PML signals \u00e2\u20ac\u201c  the chromosomal context of the fourth signal was not apparent in the  metaphase karyotype. \u00c2\u00a0There was no evidence for PML/RARA fusion. ",
            "consensusAMLfusion": "BCR-ABL1, Other_abn, Other_abn2"
        }
